Contract:
REQUEST: Which vendor emails this month look suspicious? Flag them to the AP lead.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Review the AP shared mailbox for vendor-related emails received in October 2026, identify those that look suspicious under the finance 
controls policy (look-alike domains, urgent bank-detail changes, instructions to bypass process), and send a flag email to the AP lead Priya Nair.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: An email sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in listing every suspicious vendor email found this month, with sender, date, subject, and the specific
reason it was flagged; no action taken on any flagged email.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Do not act on suspicious emails: no recording bills, no scheduling payments, no changing bank details.
  - Suspected fraud must be reported to the AP lead and then stopped.
  - Sender email domain must exactly match the vendor's registered email_domain in the ERP vendor master; look-alike domains are suspicious.
  - Urgent bank-detail change requests and instructions to bypass the normal process are suspicious regardless of domain match.
  - Use read-only ERP API only for lookups; never use admin/test endpoints.
  - Only internal email to @kestrel.in is sent (AP lead is internal), so no external-email approval is needed.
  - "This month" is interpreted as calendar month-to-date: 2026-10-01 through 2026-10-10 inclusive.
  - Do not invent email contents, vendor names, or domain matches; discover them from the mailbox and ERP.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. An email from the AP shared mailbox has been sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in with a subject indicating suspicious vendor emails and a body listing all 
suspicious emails found in October 2026 with reasons.
  C2. No vendor, bill, or payment-schedule records in the ERP were created or modified as a result of this task.
  C3. Each email classified as suspicious has a documented policy-based reason: sender domain mismatch vs ERP email_domain, urgent bank-detail change, or 
instruction to bypass process.
  C4. If no suspicious vendor emails exist in October 2026, the report to the AP lead explicitly states that no suspicious emails were found.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The AP lead is Priya Nair per the finance directory.
  - "This month" means calendar month-to-date: 2026-10-01 through 2026-10-10.
  - "Vendor emails" includes emails from external senders that appear to be from current or prospective vendors/suppliers.
  - Suspicious indicators are defined by the finance controls policy: look-alike domains, urgent bank-detail changes, and instructions to bypass normal process.
  - The operator will use the AP mailbox GUI for reading and sending mail, and the read-only ERP API for vendor lookups.
PLAN:
  S1: Identify all messages in the AP shared mailbox received between 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-10 inclusive. (done when: A list exists with message IDs, sender, 
subject, received date, and has-attachment status from the /mail inbox.)
  S2: From that list, isolate vendor-related emails and extract sender address/domain, subject, date, and any body/attachment content relevant to payment or 
bank-detail instructions. (done when: A candidate list of vendor emails has been created with parsed sender domain and content signals such as urgent bank 
changes or bypass-process language.)
  S3: For each candidate sender, use the read-only ERP API to find the matching vendor and its registered email_domain. (done when: Each candidate sender has a 
documented ERP vendor match (vendor ID and registered email_domain) or is documented as not found in ERP.)
  S4: Compare each sender domain to the ERP registered email_domain and inspect content for urgent bank-detail changes or bypass instructions; classify each 
email as suspicious or not. (done when: Every candidate vendor email has a classification and, if suspicious, a specific policy-based reason.)
  S5: Send an email to priya.nair@kestrel.in flagging all suspicious emails with details and reasons, and take no action on the flagged emails. (done when: The 
email is visible in the AP mailbox Sent folder addressed to priya.nair@kestrel.in with the correct subject and body.)
  S6: Verify that only read-only ERP queries were made and no ERP writes occurred for the vendors reviewed. (done when: The read-only API queries for involved 
vendors/bills/payments show no new or changed records compared with before the review.)
